Apple is still rocking and rolling a week into November, with five new products having launched this week and two more still on tap for next week.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/top-stories-2026-11-07.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076119" /><br/>
Things are also moving forward on the software side with Apple releasing the first betas of iOS 27.3 and related updates, bringing a number of tweaks and new features. We're also looking ahead to new products coming in the first half of 2027, so read on below for all of the details on these stories and more!<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Top Stories</h2><br/>
<h3>Apple Launched Five New Products This Week</h3><br/>
Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/05/apple-launching-five-new-products-tomorrow/">released five new products on Friday, November 6,</a> following pre-orders that opened last week, including its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/05/macbook-pro-proled-xdr-reviews/">first touchscreen MacBook Pro models</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-pro-tell-logo.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071590" /><br/>
The following new products are now available:<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li>iPad mini with OLED display and A20 Pro chip</li><br/>
<li>iMac with M6 chip</li><br/>
<li>14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 chip</li><br/>
<li>14-inch MacBook Pro with OLED touchscreen</li><br/>
<li>16-inch MacBook Pro with OLED touchscreen</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
Apple's HomeView smart home hub and updated Apple TV 4K box <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/06/two-more-apple-products-next-week/">will follow next week on Friday, November 13</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>Everything New in the iOS 27.3 Beta</h3><br/>
Apple this week <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ios-27-3-beta-features/">started testing iOS 27.3</a>, the biggest update to iOS 27 since it launched in September. iOS 27.3 includes some features Apple showed off earlier this year, and it adds all-new capabilities.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/ios_27_3_beta_1_thumb.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076093" /><br/>
Among the changes in the update are <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/03/ios-27-3-safari/">Safari tweaks</a> with a new Vertical Tabs layout option plus an Adaptive Dark Mode feature for websites that don't offer their own dark mode option, Siri AI improvements, an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/03/ios-27-3-new-standby-features-on-more-iphones/">expansion of new iPhone Duo StandBy features</a> to other iPhone models, and more.<br/>
<br/>
The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/03/ios-27-3-health-app/">revamped Health app</a> that was in the 27.2 beta for testing but removed prior to the public release has returned in 27.3 and will be seeing a public launch before the end of the year.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>Apple Alerts Stores to iPhone Duo's Display Cracking Issue</h3><br/>
In a memo shared with Apple Stores and Apple Authorized Service Providers last week, and later obtained by <em>MacRumors</em>, Apple provided technicians with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/30/apple-alerts-stores-to-iphone-duo-display-cracking/">guidance on how to diagnose and address the iPhone Duo's inner display cracking issue</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iPhone-Duo-Display-Cracking.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1074763" /><br/>
If a customer reports the issue, Apple advised technicians to inspect the iPhone Duo and repair or replace it in accordance with their standard procedures. While the instructions themselves are straightforward, the fact that Apple issued an internal memo suggests the issue is widespread enough to warrant official guidance.<br/>
<br/>
Meanwhile, Apple CEO John Ternus this week said Apple is <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/02/iphone-duo-shortages-no-end/">not able to predict when it will be able to meet demand</a> for the foldable iPhone, with <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman saying that Apple's change from its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/02/iphone-duo-november/">original plan to launch the device in November in just two countries</a> has contributed to the difficulties in meeting demand.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>Three New iPads Rumored to Launch in First Half of 2027</h3><br/>
The revamped iPad mini launching this week is one piece of Apple's tablet lineup, and <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman says the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/01/three-new-ipads-in-first-half-of-2027/">rest of the lineup should be receiving updates in the first half of next year</a>. The iPad Air will reportedly be getting an upgrade to OLED displays, while iPad Pro and base iPad updates should be more modest.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/08/iPad-Pro-2024-vs-Air-2024-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1016061" /><br/>
Before those 2027 updates, there's still some time left in 2026, and while we're not expecting any more major product announcements before the end of the year, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/02/apple-isnt-done-with-2026-heres-whats-still-coming/">plenty of previously announced hardware and software updates are still on their way</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>Here's a New Tour of Apple's HomeView Software</h3><br/>
App developer Steve Troughton-Smith over the weekend <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/31/apple-homeview-software-tour/">shared a tour of the software on Apple's upcoming HomeView smart home hub</a>. Apple has already demoed the HomeView to selected tech reporters and content creators, but Troughton-Smith offered a closer look at several features, interfaces, and apps.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/HomeView-Spotify-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075152" /><br/>
CarPlay-enabled audio and video apps from third-party developers will also be supported on HomeView, and Troughton-Smith <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/02/spotify-on-apple-homeview/">shared a look at what Spotify will look like</a> on the HomeView as well.<br/>
<br/>
We've known for quite some time that HomeView was ready to be released for quite some time while Apple waited for Siri AI to be launched as the primary interaction mechanism for it. That certainly appears to be the case as it seems the units will <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/01/apple-homeview-six-month-old-software/">initially ship with six-month-old software version 26.5</a> and will have to be updated to HomeView software version 27.2 during setup.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>Apple's Flash Storage Suppliers Are Finally 'Getting Their Revenge'</h3><br/>
<em>The Wall Street Journal</em>'s Rolfe Winkler last week reported that <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/30/apple-flash-storage-suppliers-revenge-report/">flash storage suppliers once "bullied" by Apple have been "getting their revenge" on the company</a> over the past year due to a severe memory chip shortage, which stems from AI companies building out massive data centers that utilize significant amounts of flash storage and RAM.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/04/apple-silicon-feature-joeblue.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-945652" /><br/>
As the iPhone took off, Apple became the world's largest buyer of flash storage, and naturally that gave the company a lot of leverage in negotiations. The report goes into detail about some of the hardball tactics that were employed by Apple and its former head of procurement, Tony Blevins.<br/>
<br/>
Flash suppliers now have the upper hand, however, and high demand for their chips has resulted in shortages that are expected to persist through 2030 with high prices continuing as a result.<br/>
